_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.08060349437118097,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":60.2,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.1095121095121095,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.14430300420661035,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006948018528049408,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":88.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.00052,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Solstice Advanced Materials, Inc. operates as a specialty chemicals and advanced materials company in the United States and internationally. It operates in two segments: Refrigerants & Applied Solutions (RAS), and Electronic & Specialty Materials (ESM). The RAS segment manufactures and sells low global warming potential (LGWP) refrigerants, blowing agents, solvents, and aerosol materials; and provides, aerosol propellants, cleaning solvents, pharmaceutical packaging materials, and alternative energy services under the Solstice, Genetron, and Aclar brands. The ESM segment offers electronic materials, fibers and laboratory life science chemicals for semiconductor, defense, pharmaceutical, and construction markets. This segment provides sputtering targets, lightweight high-strength fibers, and high-purity life science solutions under the Spectra, Fluka, and Hydranal brands. Solstice Advanced Materials, Inc. was incorporated in 2025 and is headquartered in Morris Plains, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David B. Sewell | CEO, President & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $948K ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $29K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Solstice Advanced Materials Inc is a large-cap basic materials business with a $10.4B market cap on $3.9B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $119M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 3 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.92\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage of 24\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 14.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 434% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.335961128907424},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 11% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 8% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"We Think You Can Look Beyond Solstice Advanced Materials' (NASDAQ:SOLS) Lackluster Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nasdaq-sols/solstice-advanced-materials/news/we-think-you-can-look-beyond-solstice-advanced-materials-nas","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482617.381,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"CenterBook Partners LP Makes New Investment in Solstice Advanced Mat $SOLS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/centerbook-partners-lp-makes-new-investment-in-solstice-advanced-mat-sols.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794075419.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.912,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Solstice Advanced Mat (SOLS) to Issue Quarterly Dividend of $0.07 on December 10th","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/solstice-advanced-mat-sols-to-issue-quarterly-dividend-of-0-07-on-decembe